    "topic": "Peace Education",
    "topicCode": "SS3-GOV-03",
    "module": "Conflict and Peace",
    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Peace</span> is more than the absence of war. It is a state of harmony, security, justice and mutual respect within and between societies. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Peace education</span> teaches people the values, attitudes and skills needed to live peacefully.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Peace</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Peace means a condition of order and calm in which individuals and groups live together without violence, fear or oppression, and where disagreements are settled by non-violent means.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. The Need for Peace</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>It protects lives and property.</li><li>It creates conditions for economic growth and development.</li><li>It allows democracy and good governance to thrive.</li><li>It encourages foreign investment and tourism.</li><li>It promotes unity, cooperation and national integration.</li><li>It allows citizens to enjoy fundamental human rights.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Ways of Promoting Peace</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Way</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Justice and rule of law</td><td>Fair treatment for all citizens</td></tr><tr><td>Equitable distribution of resources</td><td>Reduces grievances and marginalisation</td></tr><tr><td>Tolerance and dialogue</td><td>Respect for religious, ethnic and political differences</td></tr><tr><td>Good governance</td><td>Transparency, accountability and inclusion</td></tr><tr><td>Peace education</td><td>Teaching non-violence in schools, homes and religious bodies</td></tr><tr><td>Regional and international cooperation</td><td>Peacekeeping by the UN, AU and ECOWAS</td></tr><tr><td>Free and fair elections</td><td>Prevents disputes over power</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Summary:</strong> Peace is built on justice, tolerance and good governance, not merely on the absence of fighting.</div>",
