    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Foreign policy</span> is the set of principles, objectives and strategies a country uses in its relations with other countries and international bodies. It is aimed at protecting and promoting the national interest.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Factors that Influence Nigeria's Foreign Policy</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Geographical location, size and population (Nigeria is the most populous country in Africa).</li><li>Economic conditions and natural resources, especially oil.</li><li>Historical experiences such as colonialism and the civil war.</li><li>Military and technological capability.</li><li>Political ideology and the type of government in power.</li><li>The international environment, including the Cold War and global alliances.</li><li>Domestic public opinion and the interests of leaders.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Principles of Nigeria's Foreign Policy</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Africa as the centrepiece</td><td>Priority is given to African affairs</td></tr><tr><td>Non-alignment</td><td>Not joining any power bloc</td></tr><tr><td>Non-interference</td><td>Respect for the internal affairs of other states</td></tr><tr><td>Respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity</td><td>Every state is equal</td></tr><tr><td>Peaceful settlement of disputes</td><td>Use of dialogue, not force</td></tr><tr><td>Support for decolonisation and against racism</td><td>Opposition to apartheid and colonial rule</td></tr><tr><td>Promotion of international cooperation</td><td>Support for the UN, AU and ECOWAS</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Objectives of Nigeria's Foreign Policy</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Protect the sovereignty and territorial integrity of Nigeria.</li><li>Promote the well-being and dignity of Nigerians at home and abroad.</li><li>Promote African unity and economic integration.</li><li>Promote world peace and international cooperation.</li><li>Attract foreign investment and technology for development.</li><li>Oppose colonialism, apartheid and all forms of racial discrimination.</li></ul>",
