    "topic": "Millennium Development Goals (MDGs) and NEPAD",
    "topicCode": "SS3-GOV-12",
    "module": "International Development",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Millennium Development Goals (MDGs)</span> were eight time-bound development targets adopted by world leaders at the UN Millennium Summit in 2000, to be achieved by <span class=\"learn-keyword\">2015</span>. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">NEPAD</span> is an African programme for the continent's development.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. The Eight MDGs</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Target area</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Eradicate extreme poverty and hunger</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Achieve universal primary education</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Promote gender equality and empower women</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Reduce child mortality</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Improve maternal health</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Combat HIV/AIDS, malaria and other diseases</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Ensure environmental sustainability</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Develop a global partnership for development</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Achievements by 2015</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Extreme poverty fell sharply worldwide.</li><li>Primary school enrolment rose, especially for girls.</li><li>Child and maternal deaths declined.</li><li>HIV/AIDS, malaria and TB interventions expanded.</li><li>Access to safe drinking water improved.</li><li>The MDGs were succeeded by the 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) for 2030.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. NEPAD — New Partnership for Africa's Development</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">NEPAD was adopted in 2001 by the OAU (then becoming the AU), championed by Presidents Obasanjo (Nigeria), Mbeki (South Africa), Bouteflika (Algeria) and Wade (Senegal). It is a strategic framework for Africa's own development, and it became the AU's development agency (AUDA-NEPAD).</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Aims of NEPAD</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Eradicate poverty and promote sustainable growth and development.</li><li>Promote good governance, democracy and peace.</li><li>Integrate Africa into the world economy.</li><li>Promote infrastructure, agriculture, health and education.</li><li>Attract investment; the African Peer Review Mechanism (APRM) monitors members' governance.</li></ul>",
