    "topic": "E-Government, Leadership and Followership",
    "topicCode": "SS3-GOV-13",
    "module": "Governance and Leadership",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">E-government</span> is the use of information and communication technology (ICT) by government to deliver services and interact with citizens. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Leadership</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">followership</span> are the two sides of any political relationship.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning and Examples of E-Government</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">E-government means using the internet, computers and mobile technology to provide government information and services. Examples: online tax payment, e-passport and visa applications, National Identification Number (NIN) registration, online result checking and school admission portals, e-voting, and digital payment platforms such as the Treasury Single Account (TSA).</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Advantages and Disadvantages</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Advantages</th><th>Disadvantages</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Faster, cheaper and more efficient services</td><td>High cost of setting up and maintaining systems</td></tr><tr><td>Greater transparency and less corruption</td><td>Poor electricity and internet access</td></tr><tr><td>Convenience and access for citizens</td><td>Digital illiteracy; excludes the poor and rural people</td></tr><tr><td>Better record keeping and planning</td><td>Cyber crime, hacking and privacy risks</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Leadership and Followership</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">A leader is a person who guides, directs and influences others toward a goal; followers are those who accept and support the leader. Leadership is only effective when followers cooperate.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Qualities of a Good Leader</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Honesty, integrity and accountability.</li><li>Vision and the ability to plan.</li><li>Courage and decisiveness.</li><li>Fairness and impartiality.</li><li>Good communication and listening skills.</li><li>Humility and readiness to serve; ability to inspire and motivate.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Roles of Leaders and Followers</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Leaders</th><th>Followers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Make policies and laws; provide direction</td><td>Obey laws and support legitimate government</td></tr><tr><td>Maintain law, order and security</td><td>Pay taxes and take part in elections</td></tr><tr><td>Provide services and manage resources</td><td>Offer constructive criticism and hold leaders accountable</td></tr><tr><td>Represent the nation at home and abroad</td><td>Participate in community and national development</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
